From 5a63c0fd4984bf4a73122263ee59466371255015 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: oxjmo <oxjmo@localhost>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 05:45:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/7] OnePlus 6 (enchilada): the WCN3990 radio over the modem
 PIL path

redwood_wcn3990.c drives the radio as a remote processor: RPMh rail
votes, GCC clocks, reset line, then MBA/MPSS segments through the QMP
doorbells. What the probes settled across the m24-m30 series: the door-
bell word write from an EL1 AP silently vanishes (read-back stays at
its old value, no abort), a byte write on the same page takes the whole
machine down, and the behavior is identical from the ABL fastboot chain
and from a normal boot, so the difference to Android lies in the boot
chain's TZ setup, not in the EL. redwood_pcie.c is the archived root
complex probe that showed the radio lives on the SNOC, not PCIe.
